        <h2>Sources</h2>
        <ul class="sources">
          <li>PCI Security Standards Council, <a href="https://www.pcisecuritystandards.org/glossary/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Glossary</a> and <a href="https://listings.pcisecuritystandards.org/pdfs/pci_fs_data_storage.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Data Storage Do's and Don'ts</a> (a card number is cardholder data that must be rendered unreadable where stored).</li>
          <li>FTC, <a href="https://www.ftc.gov/business-guidance/resources/start-security-guide-business" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Start with Security</a> (no one can steal what you do not have).</li>
          <li>FBI Denver Field Office, <a href="https://www.fbi.gov/contact-us/field-offices/denver/news/fbi-denver-warns-of-online-file-converter-scam" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Warning on online file-converter scams</a> (March 2025; converter tools used to load malware).</li>
          <li>Smallpdf, <a href="https://smallpdf.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Privacy</a> (files permanently removed one hour after processing); iLovePDF, <a href="https://www.ilovepdf.com/help/security" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Security</a> (uploads deleted within two hours).</li>
          <li>MDN Web Docs, <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/File_API" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">File API</a> (a web app accesses files the user makes available on their own device).</li>
          <li>PDF Association, <a href="https://pdfa.org/resource/tagged-pdf-q-a/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Tagged PDF Q &amp; A</a> (software reading a PDF interprets layout rather than reading a real table).</li>
          <li>IRS, <a href="https://www.irs.gov/publications/p463" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Publication 463</a> (documentary evidence: vendor name, date, amount) and <a href="https://www.irs.gov/pub/irs-pdf/p583.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Publication 583</a> (proof of payment alone does not establish a deduction).</li>
          <li>IRS, <a href="https://www.irs.gov/businesses/small-businesses-self-employed/how-long-should-i-keep-records" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">How long should I keep records</a> (generally three years) and <a href="https://www.irs.gov/faqs/small-business-self-employed-other-business/income-expenses/income-expenses-1" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Income &amp; Expenses FAQ</a> (keep business and personal accounts separate).</li>
          <li>C+R Research, <a href="https://www.crresearch.com/blog/subscription-service-statistics-and-costs/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Subscription Service Statistics</a> (2022 survey of 1,000 US consumers: estimated 86 dollars, actual 219 dollars, gap 133 dollars a month).</li>
          <li>CFPB, <a href="https://www.consumerfinance.gov/compliance/circulars/consumer-financial-protection-circular-2023-01-unlawful-negative-option-marketing-practices/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Circular 2023-01</a> (unreasonable barriers to cancellation) and <a href="https://www.consumerfinance.gov/consumer-tools/credit-cards/how-to-fix-mistakes-in-your-credit-card-bill/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">How to fix mistakes in your credit card bill</a> (60-day dispute window).</li>
          <li>IBM, <a href="https://www.ibm.com/reports/data-breach" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Cost of a Data Breach 2025</a> (global 4.44 million, US 10.22 million, financial 5.56 million dollars); Verizon, <a href="https://www.verizon.com/about/news/2025-data-breach-investigations-report" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">2025 DBIR</a> (third-party involvement doubled to 30 percent).</li>
